  "stem": "The graph of the linear function \\(f\\) in the \\(xy\\)-plane has a slope of \\(\\frac{5}{2}\\). If \\(f(4) = 13\\), what is the value of \\(f(-2)\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "-2"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "From \\(x = 4\\) to \\(x = -2\\), \\(x\\) changes by \\(-6\\).",
    "So \\(f\\) changes by \\(\\frac{5}{2}(-6) = -15\\): \\(f(-2) = 13 - 15 = -2\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nf = 13 + Rational(5, 2)*(x - 4)\nans = f.subs(x, -2)\nassert ans == -2\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [ans]",
